 <sys:String x:Key="GuideTitle">QUICK GUIDE</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideDescription">How to use SW-MATE AI effectively</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep1">1. Open the Part/Assembly/Drawing you want to work with.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep2">2. Use AI CAD COMMAND to create, modify, or ask about the model.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep3">3. Review TASK PLAN; ✓ Verified means the Skill result was checked.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep4">4. Use MODEL INSPECTOR for a quick snapshot of actual CAD data.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep5">5. MANUAL CAD TOOLS are intended for testing and recovery.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep6">6. Ask about feature dependencies to see what depends on what and inspect design intent.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExamples">Example commands:</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample1">• Create a 160 x 100 x 12 mm plate, two Ø12 holes, fillet R8</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample2">• Change D1@Sketch1 to 70 mm</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample3">• What is the current material?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample4">• What is the overall size?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample5">• What are the feature dependencies in this part?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideTip">Tip: clearer dimensions, positions, and target objects help the Agent build a more accurate plan.</sys:String>
